  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Requirements**\n\nI\'ve realized the initial assumption about building a Streamlit interface was off-base. The actual task is to construct a web application for the IGCSE geography question generator, but the user requested a Streamlit interface! I need to ensure clarity on the target development technology.\n\n\n**Reconciling Technology Choices**\n\nI\'ve clarified the development environment and realized I must use TypeScript and React, not Streamlit as initially assumed. My new plan is to build a React application using Vite and Tailwind to create a user interface that aligns with the requested Streamlit-like experience. The UI will feature the core IGCSE question generation system: Paper selection (Paper 1/2), topic dropdowns (dependent on paper), and command word selection (Explain/Evaluate/Justify) while interacting with the Gemini API.\n\n\n**Defining API Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the Google Generative AI API, deciding on `@google/genai` to handle the model interactions. I\'m building a function to format the user\'s selections and send the query to the model. I am thinking of using three markdown containers for the question and the mark scheme and the sentence starters. I need to handle server-side secret API keys, so I am going to setup full-stack Express + Vite.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 955780303
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
