the header component with the Bento grid design. I\'m adapting the existing header structure, aiming for consistency. I\'m focusing on preserving the current responsiveness and visual elements while aligning it with the Bento grid\'s look and feel. The `min-h-screen bg-[#f8fafc] text-slate-900 font-sans flex flex-col` structure is maintained, and I\'m updating the header\'s styling to fit seamlessly.\n\n\n**Styling Form Controls**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on styling the form controls within the sidebar. I\'ve updated the dropdown styles with classes for background, border, rounded corners, text size, focus ring, outline, padding, and width. The labels are also updated to fit, with bold text and capitalization.\n\n\n**Defining Button Appearance**\n\nI\'m now detailing button and output panel styles. Button styling now uses classes for width, background, hover states, text color and weight, padding, rounded corners, shadow, and transition effects, with disabled states. I\'m structuring output panels based on loading or result states, using Bento grid elements for result display and a centered layout with rounded corners for loading or no result states.\n\n\n**Integrating Question Styles**\n\nI\'m now integrating the question and mark scheme components, focusing on Bento grid classes. The plan is to maintain the current HTML structure while injecting the appropriate grid column spans to achieve the intended layout. I\'m focusing on preserving their respective background and text colors and markdown rendering, along with the title elements.\n\n\n**Adjusting Styling Components**\n\nI\'m now comparing styles in light and dark modes, particularly focusing on the \"prose\" styling class. I\'m updating `App.tsx` to match the light mode requirements. I\'m removing the `prose-invert` class in `App.tsx`, and making some adjustments to the sentence starters component. I\'m working on the `prose prose-slate` in the light mode. For the sentence starters, I am focusing on the custom styling shown.\n\n\n**Refining Header Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the header styling into the overall design. I\'m focusing on the component in `src/App.tsx`, updating the background, text, and overall appearance to fit the existing style. I\'m focusing on preserving responsiveness and functionality while enhancing the visual integration. I\'ve updated the background and border classes. I\'m also ensuring the gradient and icon are correctly styled.\n\n```\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Content Section**\n\nI\'m now styling the main content area, making significant layout changes. I\'ve switched to a flexbox structure within a grid, using `lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 p-4 sm:p-6 lg:p-8 flex-1`. I\'m integrating the question components with the bento classes, ensuring responsiveness across all screen sizes. I\'m focusing on preserving markdown rendering and maintaining consistency with the overall design. I\'m prioritizing optimal viewing with overflow adjustments.\n\n\n**Optimizing Responsive Grid**\n\nI\'m now implementing responsiveness across various screen sizes within the content section. I\'m focusing on refining the grid layout using responsive classes like `lg:grid-cols-12` to ensure consistent display on all devices. I\'m prioritizing clear and readable markdown rendering, fine-tuning the components\' grid spans. My focus remains on ensuring a smooth user experience across a range of devices.\n\n\n**Refining Styling Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the styling for the form controls. I\'ve updated the styles for the dropdown, specifically targeting the topic and command word dropdowns. I\'m focusing on consistency. I\'ve updated the background color, added borders and rounded corners, and increased text size. I\'ve also implemented focus rings, outline effects, padding, and ensured full width. Labels are styled with bold text and capitalisation. I\'m focusing on disabled and required states as well.\n\n\n"
