  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Approach**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the core request: removing the badge and avatar, then integrating a dark mode toggle into the header\'s design. This necessitates a precise analysis of the UI structure to locate and eliminate those specific elements while architecting a seamless spot for the new dark mode control.\n\n\n**Implementing Dark Mode**\n\nI\'m now focused on enabling dark mode. Tailwind v4\'s `dark:` variant handles this, either via system preference or a class toggle. I\'m considering using manual state mapping with a wrapper element and a `.dark` class, and implementing this in `index.css`. I\'ve identified the necessary selectors, specifically targeting the avatar and badge, for removal or styling changes based on the mode.\n\n\n**Refining Dark Mode Logic**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the dark mode implementation. Initially, I was looking at manual state mapping, but I\'ve reverted to the standard Tailwind approach, which involves wrapping the main content in a `dark` class, and using a state variable `[isDark, setIsDark]` for the toggle and conditional `dark:` prefixes. I have to go through and add these `dark:` prefixes to all Tailwind classes to enable dark mode, and removing the hardcoded styles.\n\n\n**Adapting Styles for Dark Mode**\n\nI\'m making good progress updating the Tailwind classes for dark mode. I\'m adding `dark:` prefixes systematically: for example, `text-slate-900` becomes `dark:text-slate-100` and `bg-white` turns into `dark:bg-slate-900`. I\'m also considering the Sentence Starters section, and I\'ve decided to keep the dark box styling consistent across modes, or adapt as needed. Finally, I\'m replacing right-aligned header items with a toggle button using Lucide icons.\n\n\n**Refining Dark Mode Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating the dark mode toggle into `App.tsx`. I\'m using a state variable, `isDark`, to conditionally apply the \"dark\" class to the root `div` element. After reviewing Tailwind documentation, I\'m setting `document.documentElement.classList.toggle(\'dark\')` in a `useEffect` hook to manage the `html` class directly. Finally, I\'m going through and applying light/dark color equivalents systematically, such as replacing `bg-[#f8fafc]` with `bg-slate-50`.\n\n\n**Applying Dark Mode**\n\nI\'m now focusing on systematic style updates. I\'ve updated background, text, and border colors with `dark:` variants for dark mode, like replacing `text-slate-900` with `dark:text-slate-100`. I\'m refining the \"Sentence Starters\" section for dark mode, adjusting background and border styles. I\'m also ensuring the text content is readable in dark mode with `dark:prose-invert`. Next, I will add `Moon` and `Sun` imports from `lucide-react`.\n\n\n**Integrating the Toggle**\n\nI\'ve integrated the dark mode toggle and streamlined its functionality. I\'ve removed the generic user div and the \"Gemini 1.5 Flash Connected\" div. I added the `isDark` state variable and a `useEffect` hook to toggle the `dark` class on the `document.documentElement`. I\'m replacing the classes for dark mode and am testing thoroughly.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Toggle**\n\nI\'ve got the dark mode toggle button fully implemented, using `Sun` and `Moon` icons from `lucide-react` within a button component and applying `dark` class toggling to the document element. I\'m now systematically updating the style classes for elements throughout the application to ensure complete dark mode compatibility. I am going through the aside elements and applying the dark variants.\n\n\n**Updating Style Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific style refinements. I\'ve updated several key UI elements. For the content container, I\'ve adjusted the background, borders, and rounded corners to provide better visual distinction. I\'ve ensured a consistent color palette by updating text and background colors with appropriate `dark:` variants for readability and visual appeal. I\'m also addressing the output containers, applying dark mode-specific styles for both background and text to ensure a clear distinction.\n\n\n\n**Revising Style Updates**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dark mode style updates. I\'ve updated the \"Mark Scheme\" with `bg-white dark:bg-slate-900`, `border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800`, and `text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300`. For \"Sentence Starters\", I opted for `bg-slate-900 dark:bg-slate-950` and `border-slate-800`. Finally, I\'ve imported `Copy`, `RefreshCw`, `Send`, `Loader2`, `BookOpen`, `Sun`, and `Moon` from `lucide-react`.\n\n\n**Finalizing Theme Integration**\n\nI\'ve got the `App` component\'s structure in place now. I\'m using `isDark` with `useState` and toggling the `dark` class on `documentElement` inside `useEffect`, enabling automatic style switching. The header uses `light` and `dark` color themes and includes a button that toggles `isDark` using `Sun` and `Moon` lucide icons. I\'m testing the integration.\n\n\n**Refining Aside Components**\n\nI\'m now implementing updates to the aside components to achieve better visual integration. I\'ve updated the aside with a light and dark theme, including background, border, and text colors for improved readability. I\'ve focused on ensuring the color contrast is adequate and consistent across all states, and the aside is now using a `p-6` to provide the padding and maintain consistent padding from other components. Next, I\'m focusing on the select components.\n\n\n\n**Adjusting Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing targeted style refinements for several components. Specifically, I\'m updating the System Specs box using `bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/30`, `border-dashed border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700`, and related text classes. I\'m also styling the Awaiting Parameters box with updated `bg-white dark:bg-slate-900`, `border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800`, as well as icon and text color adjustments.\n\n\n**Refining Component Styling**\n\nI\'m now refining loading and question section components for dark mode compatibility. I\'m adding `dark:` variants for colors, borders, and backgrounds to maintain consistent styling across themes. I am focusing on providing a good visual distinction and using proper color contrast to ensure readability in dark mode. Finally, I\'ll update the text colors.\n\n\n**Enhancing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating dark mode styling across key interface elements. I\'ve updated the Sentence Starters section to retain its darker appearance for better contrast in all modes. I\'ve also carefully applied `dark:` variants to the Mark Scheme\'s background, border, and text, ensuring visual consistency across themes. I\'m focusing on text color adjustments for the prose sections.\n\n\n"
