  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising Control Panel Layout**\n\nI\'m currently working on adjusting the control panel\'s layout. My focus is on aligning the dropdowns and generate button to the left, which I\'ve started implementing. Simultaneously, I\'m integrating a countdown timer on the right side. The centered approach will be eliminated and replaced by these two independent sections.\n\n\n**Implementing Timer Controls**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating a `TeacherTimer` component into the top controls container, and now it\'s successfully rendered. I\'ve switched the container to a column-based layout that adapts to a row layout at a medium breakpoint, with space for the form and timer sections. The timer component is functional.\n\n\n**Developing Timer Logic**\n\nI\'ve been creating the core timer functionality using React hooks. I\'ve got `isActive`, `inputMinutes`, `timeLeft` and their corresponding state-setting functions set up. I\'ve implemented `useEffect` to manage the interval and clear it on unmount or state changes. The `toggleTimer`, `resetTimer`, and `handleSetTime` functions are also written.\n\n\n**Refining Timer Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the timer\'s display format. I\'m formatting the `timeLeft` state into a \"MM:SS\" string for the display. I\'m ensuring it\'s always two digits long by padding with a leading zero if necessary. I\'ve also incorporated the input to set the minutes for the timer.\n\n\n**Integrating Timer Controls**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated the pause and start, and reset buttons within the `<TeacherTimer>` component. I\'m dynamically rendering either \"Pause\" or \"Start\" on the button based on timer state. I\'ve also incorporated a reset button. Each button has distinct styles, reflecting active or inactive states using Tailwind classes. Their behaviour correctly updates the state.\n\n\n**Adjusting Top Bar Elements**\n\nI\'m now revising the top bar layout to match the requested design. I\'m focusing on aligning the dropdowns and the generate button correctly. I\'ve reconfigured the flexbox to accommodate the form and button in a columnar manner for smaller screens, transitioning to a row-based layout at wider viewports. I\'m also preparing to import new icons from `lucide-react`. Finally, I\'ve relocated the `TeacherTimer` component outside of the form.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 34
      nanos: 936012513
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
