djusting Horizontal Space**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the `TeacherTimer` component should consume the remaining horizontal space. I\'m exploring setting `TeacherTimer` to `w-full xl:w-80 shrink-0` to control its width and prevent it from expanding beyond its intended size. This, in conjunction with flex properties, should resolve the space allocation issue and allow for a balanced layout.\n\n\n**Refining the Timer Element**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `TeacherTimer`\'s attributes, making sure it stretches vertically when necessary, but otherwise keeps its natural height. By setting its `w-full xl:w-[320px] shadow-sm shrink-0`, I am hoping it will take the horizontal space available. I\'ve updated the top controls structure, and now the `TeacherTimer` has been given `h-full` if needed.\n\n\n"
