  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing TeacherTimer\'s CSS**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on TeacherTimer\'s CSS, specifically how the dark mode toggle integrates with the branding. Examining the classes, I see flexbox for layout, centering elements. The light and dark background styles and borders are immediately apparent, crucial for visual consistency. I\'m noting the use of utility classes.\n\n\n**Refining TeacherTimer\'s Structure**\n\nI\'ve streamlined the `TeacherTimer` component\'s structure. The goal is a simpler, more compact toolbar-like widget appearance. Removed the large paddings and borders for a cleaner look. The new CSS focuses on rounded full backgrounds, and reduced padding and simplified border styles for a more subtle integration with the overall UI.\n\n\n**Implementing Timer Controls**\n\nI\'m now integrating the timer controls, aiming for a clean, compact design. I\'ve used flexbox for the button layout. I\'ve incorporated icons for play/pause and reset functionality, and applied transition effects. I\'m focusing on hover states for visual feedback, using conditional styling to toggle between active and inactive states. Next I need to move these to a collapsible UI, with the chevron icons.\n\n\n"
